  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6bdc-b342-b8e6-6d91" name="Numidian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #34 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Numidians of North Africa are the people later known as Berbers or Moors. They formed various tribal groupings which at various times might coalesce under the leadership of a powerful ruler, but equally they might fight each other, often by taking opposing sides in someone else’s struggle. Numidians provided excellent cavalry for Carthaginian and Roman armies and the latter trained infantry forces for them, so that while early armies would comprise cavalry and skirmishers, later ones might contain quite sizeable numbers of formed foot, including imitation legionaries. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Numidian]
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: At least 25% Infantry: Up to 50% Elephants: Up to 1 per 750 points</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
